[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765403887","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115093#issuecomment-3765403887","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115093","id":3765403887,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gb4Dv","user":{"login":"Kn1feKillz","id":251789733,"node_id":"U_kgDODwIBpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/251789733?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz","html_url":"https://github.com/Kn1feKillz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T15:22:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T15:22:55Z","body":"I may not understand the idea, but how can a copy constructor be implicit? \r\n```cpp\r\nHashMap<int, int> other = hashmap; // implicit copy, now illegal\r\n```\r\nThis is specifically a call to the copy constructor; nothing else can be implied here.\r\nThis is not an operator of casting to another type that could be implicit, but a form of initialization, that is, a call to the constructor.\r\n\r\nIt seems to me that this is unnecessary verbosity, which makes it difficult to read.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765403887/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765415975","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115093#issuecomment-3765415975","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115093","id":3765415975,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gb7An","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T15:35:50Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T15:35:50Z","body":"> I may not understand the idea, but how can a copy constructor be implicit?\r\n> \r\n> ```c++\r\n> HashMap<int, int> other = hashmap; // implicit copy, now illegal\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> This is specifically a call to the copy constructor; nothing else can be implied here. This is not an operator of casting to another type that could be implicit, but a form of initialization, that is, a call to the constructor.\r\n> \r\n> It seems to me that this is unnecessary verbosity, which makes it difficult to read.\r\n\r\nThe idea is that the copy constructor, for large / expensive types like `HashMap`, is rarely useful and usually something to be avoided:\r\n- If you want to assign it to a local variable for quick access, usually reference semantics are preferable.\r\n- If you have constructed it recently and want to put it somewhere, usually move semantics are preferable.\r\n\r\nYou can see unintended copies happening all over the changelog, for example:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n// This should be a reference, no copy is needed\r\nHashMap<StringName, String> global_groups = ProjectSettings::get_singleton()->get_global_groups_list();\r\nfor (const KeyValue<StringName, String> &E : global_groups) {\r\n\tr_options->push_back(E.key.operator String().quote());\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThese kinds of mistakes can cause loss of performance, and make it hard to understand what exactly is happening in the code.\r\nIn the example above it may be easy to understand regardless:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nHashMap<int, int> other = hashmap; // implicit copy\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut in other cases it may not be so obvious:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nLocalVector<HashMap<int, int>> maps;\r\n\r\nHashMap<int, int> data = { ... };\r\nmaps.push_back(data); // implicit copy due to call, std::move should have been used\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765415975/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765549080","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115093#issuecomment-3765549080","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115093","id":3765549080,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gcbgY","user":{"login":"Kn1feKillz","id":251789733,"node_id":"U_kgDODwIBpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/251789733?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz","html_url":"https://github.com/Kn1feKillz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T17:56:50Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T17:56:50Z","body":"No, the idea of ​​using something other than copying is perfectly clear. I don't understand how a different form of constructor call is supposed to prevent unnecessary copying of an object. I mean, yes, people should use a reference when copying is possible, but how do we avoid this by \"explicitly\" calling copy?\r\n\r\nI mean, if someone forgets to call std::move() on a function argument, the rule that copying must be called \"explicitly\" won't help, will it?\r\n\r\nAnd if this is going to be a review rule, why not just make it a review rule to avoid copying, given that the code doesn't use \"auto\" and the examples you showed are pretty obvious.\r\n\r\nWhat I'm trying to get at is that this won't stop those who aren't careful about copying from making mistakes, but it will clutter the code and can lead to other types of errors, such as copy-pasta.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765549080/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765555420","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115093#issuecomment-3765555420","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115093","id":3765555420,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gcdDc","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T18:03:54Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T18:03:54Z","body":"> And if this is going to be a review rule, why not just make it a review rule to avoid copying, given that the code doesn't use \"auto\" and the examples you showed are pretty obvious.\r\n\r\nReviews are the biggest bottleneck of the project. If we want to improve on this we need to get more people reviewing. Reviewers should not need to have this level of C++ code vision IMO\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765555420/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765566035","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115093#issuecomment-3765566035","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115093","id":3765566035,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gcfpT","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T18:15:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T18:18:36Z","body":"> I mean, if someone forgets to call std::move() on a function argument, the rule that copying must be called \"explicitly\" won't help, will it?\r\n\r\nIt will! Because it will no longer be possible to call the following:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nLocalVector<HashMap<int, int>> maps;\r\n\r\nHashMap<int, int> data = { ... };\r\n\r\n// Impossible after the PR, the compiler will refuse to compile this\r\nmaps.push_back(data);\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut the following will work:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n// This will work.\r\nmaps.push_back(std::move(data));\r\n\r\n// This will compile, but requires an active decision from the PR author to copy the map\r\n// That should already stop many accidental copies taking place, because most will reject\r\n// the idea of the map having to be copied here.\r\n// Additionally, reviewers will see it as an obvious performance trap\r\nmaps.push_back(HashMap<int, int>(data)); \r\n```\r\n\r\n> What I'm trying to get at is that this won't stop those who aren't careful about copying from making mistakes, but it will clutter the code and can lead to other types of errors, such as copy-pasta.\r\n\r\nI think you may overestimate how often `HashMap` instances need to be copied. I know now, from making this PR, and I can confidently say that it is maybe 5 times in our whole codebase at most. The rest of the copies are accidental.\r\n\r\nSo, since the method won't be used very often, it will also not \"clutter\" the codebase.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765566035/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765570590","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115093#issuecomment-3765570590","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115093","id":3765570590,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gcgwe","user":{"login":"Kn1feKillz","id":251789733,"node_id":"U_kgDODwIBpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/251789733?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz","html_url":"https://github.com/Kn1feKillz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T18:20:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T18:20:06Z","body":"> > And if this is going to be a review rule, why not just make it a review rule to avoid copying, given that the code doesn't use \"auto\" and the examples you showed are pretty obvious.\r\n> \r\n> Reviews are the biggest bottleneck of the project. If we want to improve on this we need to get more people reviewing. Reviewers should not need to have this level of C++ code vision IMO\r\n\r\nBut this update also requires reviewers to know that the copy constructor is called this way, which means that they also know about the regular call to the copy constructor.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765570590/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765572173","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115093#issuecomment-3765572173","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115093","id":3765572173,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gchJN","user":{"login":"Kn1feKillz","id":251789733,"node_id":"U_kgDODwIBpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/251789733?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz","html_url":"https://github.com/Kn1feKillz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kn1feKillz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T18:21:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T18:21:46Z","body":"> The rest of the copies are accidental.\r\n\r\nOkay, I get it. I reviewed the PR and saw that the copy constructor is declared explicit. For some reason, I missed that. That could work, yes.\r\n\r\nOn the topic of performance, I'd also add the ability to pass arguments to containers, like a vector, by right reference. There are no methods for that. I'll try to write a proposal about it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765572173/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3771762574","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115093#issuecomment-3771762574","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115093","id":3771762574,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g0IeO","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T09:00:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T09:00:23Z","body":"Agree with this on the principle of aiming to make expensive operations explicit and more obvious to reviewers / contributors.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3771762574/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3829439637","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115093#issuecomment-3829439637","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115093","id":3829439637,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kQJyV","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T22:00:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T22:00:37Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3829439637/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]